From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AP: free a non-AP MLD on all its links at a BSS deinit

Depends on 878-AP-add-hostapd_bss_stop_ap-for-a-stop-that-keeps-the.patch.

hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free() flushes the stations of the link in the
driver and sends the broadcast Deauthentication. mac80211 then drops
every non-AP MLD that holds the link with all its links, and the
Deauthentication ends the association of such a non-AP MLD on all its
links. hostapd_free_stas() frees only the link STA of a non-AP MLD
whose association link is another link of the AP MLD, so DISABLE of
that link left the non-AP MLD associated and authorized on its
association link, and its next association failed.

hostapd_bss_stop_ap() already frees such a non-AP MLD on all its links
first. Share that part with hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free().

Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1961,10 +1961,19 @@ static int hostapd_flush_old_stations(st
 }
 
 
-void hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+static void hostapd_bss_stas_leave(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
+	hostapd_free_link_sta_mlds(hapd);
+#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
 	hostapd_free_stas(hapd);
 	hostapd_flush_old_stations(hapd, WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING);
+}
+
+
+void hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
+{
+	hostapd_bss_stas_leave(hapd);
 #ifdef CONFIG_WEP
 	hostapd_clear_wep(hapd);
 #endif /* CONFIG_WEP */
@@ -1975,12 +1984,7 @@ void hostapd_bss_deinit_no_free(struct h
  * free them first. The keys of the BSS stay for the next start. */
 void hostapd_bss_stop_ap(struct hostapd_data *hapd)
 {
-#ifdef CONFIG_IEEE80211BE
-	if (hapd->conf->mld_ap)
-		hostapd_free_link_sta_mlds(hapd);
-#endif /* CONFIG_IEEE80211BE */
-	hostapd_free_stas(hapd);
-	hostapd_flush_old_stations(hapd, WLAN_REASON_DEAUTH_LEAVING);
+	hostapd_bss_stas_leave(hapd);
 	hostapd_drv_stop_ap(hapd);
 	hapd->beacon_set_done = 0;
 }
